1
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,786
A supplier discontinues one chip. Which products use it?

2
00:00:07,826 --> 00:00:11,094
What does it cost us? Who needs to act? Today,

3
00:00:11,134 --> 00:00:14,329
that takes days of spreadsheets and meetings.

4
00:00:14,369 --> 00:00:16,630
RippleOps answers it in minutes.

5
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,217
Here is a supplier's end-of-life notice. Gemini reads it,

6
00:00:22,257 --> 00:00:24,143
extracts the part, the change type,

7
00:00:24,183 --> 00:00:27,169
the last-time-buy date and the recommended replacement,

8
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:29,590
and validates them against our product data.

9
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:34,722
Now, nine Google ADK agents take the case.

10
00:00:34,762 --> 00:00:40,025
An impact analyst sizes the exposure. Then two teams work in parallel:

11
00:00:40,065 --> 00:00:42,525
a sourcing team scouts suppliers,

12
00:00:42,565 --> 00:00:46,389
while three due-diligence agents check performance,

13
00:00:46,429 --> 00:00:48,510
sanctions and supplier news.

14
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:53,131
And a planning team forecasts demand and re-plans production.

15
00:00:53,171 --> 00:00:58,131
Every step streams live. A coordinator writes the executive brief.

16
00:01:02,761 --> 00:01:06,631
Each finding carries a Gemini badge and a figures-verified check.

17
00:01:06,671 --> 00:01:11,563
A grounding guardrail compares every number the agents write with the tool output,

18
00:01:11,603 --> 00:01:15,112
and replaces anything it cannot trace with calculated text.

19
00:01:17,402 --> 00:01:20,814
BigQuery Graph traces the chip through every bill of materials:

20
00:01:20,854 --> 00:01:22,677
twelve products in three families,

21
00:01:22,717 --> 00:01:25,416
four point two million dollars of revenue exposed,

22
00:01:25,456 --> 00:01:27,334
and only fifty-eight days of stock.

23
00:01:27,374 --> 00:01:30,019
Our Edge Controller Pro uses four of these chips,

24
00:01:30,059 --> 00:01:31,992
through two separate assembly paths.

25
00:01:34,282 --> 00:01:37,708
Anyone can ask a follow-up question. Why is P300 high risk?

26
00:01:37,748 --> 00:01:40,527
The assistant answers by calling the same tools,

27
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:43,876
so every number in its answer comes from the calculation,

28
00:01:43,916 --> 00:01:44,992
not from the model.

29
00:01:48,070 --> 00:01:52,120
Sourcing found five options. Crescent Semiconductor scores highest,

30
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:53,890
as a long-term second source.

31
00:01:53,930 --> 00:01:56,819
A cheap clone is blocked by sanctions screening,

32
00:01:56,859 --> 00:01:59,444
and broker stock is flagged as bridge-only.

33
00:01:59,484 --> 00:02:01,214
Underneath sits the evidence:

34
00:02:01,254 --> 00:02:04,754
four quarters of delivery and quality data, supplier news,

35
00:02:04,794 --> 00:02:07,500
and a sanctions screen across every supplier.

36
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:13,322
The demand planner forecasts with BigQuery's TimesFM model.

37
00:02:13,362 --> 00:02:17,014
The production planner re-plans thirteen weeks with OR-Tools,

38
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:18,164
tests a bridge buy,

39
00:02:18,204 --> 00:02:23,249
and lifts fill rate on the affected products from sixty-four to one hundred percent.

40
00:02:23,289 --> 00:02:26,154
It lists exactly what changes on the shop floor:

41
00:02:26,194 --> 00:02:28,454
which products switch to the new chip,

42
00:02:28,494 --> 00:02:32,449
and which move to the flex line. The agent only proposes the plan.

43
00:02:32,489 --> 00:02:33,781
A planner approves it.

44
00:02:37,771 --> 00:02:41,206
Want to test a decision first? Switching to the successor chip,

45
00:02:41,246 --> 00:02:44,131
with copper up twelve percent and freight up fifteen,

46
00:02:44,171 --> 00:02:47,441
pushes five products below our twenty percent margin target.

47
00:02:49,731 --> 00:02:52,441
Finally, every department gets its next move.

48
00:02:52,481 --> 00:02:56,047
Procurement secures the last-time buy and the bridge stock.

49
00:02:56,087 --> 00:03:00,325
Engineering validates the new chip. Operations runs the approved plan,

50
00:03:00,365 --> 00:03:04,481
and finance reviews pricing. Every action cites the facts behind it.

51
00:03:06,771 --> 00:03:09,935
Under the hood, it all runs on Google Cloud.

52
00:03:09,975 --> 00:03:13,358
The web app and the agent API run on Cloud Run.

53
00:03:13,398 --> 00:03:16,489
Gemini on Vertex AI powers nine ADK agents.

54
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:18,820
BigQuery holds the product data,

55
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:22,024
BigQuery Graph traces the bill of materials,

56
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:26,757
AI dot FORECAST predicts demand, and OR-Tools optimizes the plan.

57
00:03:26,797 --> 00:03:29,961
AI reasons; deterministic engines calculate.

58
00:03:32,785 --> 00:03:36,936
One change. Every impact. One decision.
